From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JMUtechnologies <209723632+JMUtechnologies@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:10:58 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] PS5-ECAM's Switch 2 side: EglantinePS5 as its child runtime,
 with the shared in-game menu

PS5-ECAM (PPSA99360) carries this program as eglantine/eboot.bin and starts its Switch 2 side's games
in it (EDEN_ECAM_CHILD, set by PS5-ECAM's tools/build-eglantine.sh):
- Its folder is /app0/eglantine; its Lapy helper is built for PPSA99360 (EDEN_ECAM_TITLE_ID).
- The game and the side's settings come as --rom, --exit-after-game, --ecam-session and --ecam-setting
  key=value, or from /data/eglantineps5/ps5ecam-launch-request.txt where LoadExec drops them, and
  apply over this program's own for that session.
- PS5-ECAM's in-game menu (its port/eden/ingame.h, ecam.cmake with Dear ImGui) is compiled in and drawn
  in the Vulkan present pass (vulkan_ecam_composite.inc), on Touchpad click + Options, its settings
  applied at once and Quit to library going back; the session and result files follow the data root
  PS5-ECAM chose (--ecam-session).
- When its game ends it starts PS5-ECAM's /app0/eboot.bin again, which opens on the side it left.
